{"reference":"Isaiah 43","book":"Isaiah","chapter":43,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A New Homecoming","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Verses 14–21 belong to Isaiah 40–55’s announcement of comfort and return from Babylon. Their images of a path through the sea and of water in the wilderness present that return as a new homecoming shaped by creation and exodus imagery. This promise of return does not imply that the trauma of displacement or conflict after return simply disappeared.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 43:14-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_043_0d3ddd5067fbd94be0f3e305"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A Manuscript Witness to Isaiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The Great Isaiah Scroll is an almost complete witness to all sixty-six chapters of Isaiah. It broadly aligns with the Masoretic tradition while containing thousands of spelling and substantive differences; other Isaiah manuscripts and interpretive writings from Qumran also show that the book was actively transmitted and interpreted.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_043_eea63f2cbb620e019a4d7297"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}